 /* Short H6 commands need finer steps than the microsecond delay.
- * Keep the high pulse free of maskable interrupts. The low wait has a minimum.
+ * The timer stops deliberately BELOW the target (H6_PULSE_TRIM_COUNTS), and
+ * H6_COMP() adds the rest as literal NOPs at 20.83 ns each. The poll
+ * detection quantises the timer part to roughly one loop period, but the
+ * NOP tail is exact, so one calibration lands the pulse on nominal.
+ * Maskable interrupts stay disabled while the pulse is high; the low wait
+ * only has a minimum, so it keeps the coarse delay.
  */
 #define H6_PULSE_COUNTS_PER_US  48
